   Div Water Sci; WHO UNEP Global Environm Monitoring Syst; Severn Trent
   Water; Entec Europe Ltd; NIREX UK Ltd; Environm Agcy},
Abstract = {Mauritius is a volcanic basaltic oceanic island having a highly
   heterogeneous hydrogeological structure. A conceptual groundwater flow
   model developed for the northern aquifer of the island, based on the
   concept of hydrostatigraphic units, indicated that localised regions of
   highly heterogeneous properties have major influence on the general
   groundwater flow pattern. A three dimensional picture of the aquifer on
   a regional basis does not highlight these localised heterogeneity.
   Detailed localised studies are needed to characterise the degree of
   influence of these features on the regional groundwater flow of this
   area.},
