   Div Water Sci; WHO UNEP Global Environm Monitoring Syst; Severn Trent
   Water; Entec Europe Ltd; NIREX UK Ltd; Environm Agcy},
Abstract = {The region of Berlin is dominated by Pleistoceniec sediments. Coarse to
   fine grained sands form a multiaquifer system with tills as aquiclude in
   intercallation. Clofibric acid, a medicament was detected first in
   groundwater samples of different depths from the sewage farms south of
   Berlin. The acid had passed even through the aquicludes. Later it was
   detected together with other medicine in the drinking water produced
   from Berlin water works. Some sewage farms of Berlin are situated in the
   catchment area of the production wells. Drained water from the sewage
   Farms reaches the river Spree upstream of Berlin. The river water is
   used for artificial recharge in large areas surrounded by water wells.
   Some wells of the public water works produce bank filtered groundwater.
   The research target is the identification of more medicaments and the
   determination of the pathway.},
