Abstract = {Simulation of additional exploitation of 35,000 m(3)/d using the finite
   difference method (MODFLOW) has shown a decline of the piezometric head,
   which is accompanied by saltwater intrusion in the north west of the
   aquifer system. The inflow across boundaries increases by about 20,000
   m(3)/d and sea water intrusion advance in the north west is suspected to
   contribute to this input. In addition to sea water intrusion,
   agricultural practices are also a threat to the resource quality.},
