Abstract = {A methodology for estimating groundwater protection value has been
   developed, aimed at identifying the groundwater resources which are most
   valuable for a society and therefore most important to protect. The
   methodology was applied in the Managua groundwater system in Nicaragua.
   A map indicating protection value was produced with the help of the
   geographical information system IDRISI. Through this method it was
   possible to identify the most valuable groundwater resources which need
   protection based on potential quantities one could extract or areas
   which are the most sensitive to changes in groundwater protection.},
