   (IC3E), Shanghai, PEOPLES R CHINA, MAR 14-16, 2019},
Organization = {Int Soc Environm Informat Sci; Asia Pacific Inst Sci \& Engn; Xiamen
   Univ Technol; Fujian Smart City Assoc},
Abstract = {Single Particle Aerosol Mass Spectrometry (SPAMS) is used to
   investigated a heavy haze process in Weinan,2017. Firstly, the fine
   particles (PM2.5) using ART-2a was analysed and clustered into 8
   classes: organic carbon (OC), organics and elemental carbon combined
   particles (ECOC), elemental carbon (EC), heavy metal (HM), high
   molecular organic carbon (HOC), K-rich, levoglucosan (Lev) and dust.
   Secondly, positive matrix factorization (PMF) was used to identify the
   sources of PM2.5. Results from PMF showed that the main six sources of
   PM2.5 were coal-fired (38.48\%), secondary (19.19\%), biomass burning
   (15.04\%), industry (9.28\%), traffic ( 5.02\%), and dust (5.00\%). And
   it is obvious that the major cause of the atmospheric heavy haze is an
   unfavorable meteorological conditions such as high humidity and low wind
   speed, as well as coal-fired pollution and secondary pollution caused by
   heating and industrial production.},
