   - Perspectives from Business in Asia, Hong Kong, PEOPLES R CHINA, NOV
   17, 2006},
Organization = {TU Bergakademie Freiberg; Hong Kong Univ, Ctr Urban Planning \& Environm
   Management; German Acad Exchange Serv Fdn; German Ind \& Commerce; Off
   European Commiss Hong Kong \& Macao; CSR Asia},
Abstract = {Lean production is one of the most important production modes. The core
   of lean production is to reduce and eliminate ultimately all forms of
   wastes and achieve a very low level of inventory and the highest
   customer satisfaction. When lean production is implemented, the
   situation which must be faced is how to choose the best control
   strategy. This paper intends to review the KANBAN strategy, the CONWIP
   (Constant Work in Process) strategy and the Hybrid production control
   strategy, which may be named as the integrated KANBAN-CONWIP strategy in
   the frame of lean production. Then, a generic model which includes the
   above three control strategies and the corresponding genetic algorithm
   based solution are presented. After qualitative and quantitative
   comparison, a simulation is performed to provide an appropriate
   production control strategy. The author recommends important decision
   variables which influence the performance of production.},
