   European Commiss Hong Kong \& Macao; CSR Asia},
Abstract = {Nonlinear analysis of value chain, which has been introduced into the
   field of decision-making for sustainable development in recent years, is
   an important theory for the green reengineering of tourism enterprises.
   However, the present research is focusing mainly on static qualitative
   analyses, which can not provide the quantitative reference. This paper
   studies the added value resulting from every step along a value chain,
   and proposes a quantitative equation, which is a kind of ``Logistic{''}
   equation, to calculate the added value. The equation can explain the
   ``smiling curve{''}, which has been used to explain the source of
   value-added chain.},
