   Management; German Acad Exchange Serv Fdn; German Ind \& Commerce; Off
   European Commiss Hong Kong \& Macao; CSR Asia},
Abstract = {The evaluation of corporate environmental performance with weight
   assignment as a key step in multi-attribute decisions making, is one
   important issue in corporate environmental management. Generally,
   pair-wise comparison matrix is used in this procedure, but the entries
   are always affected by various factors and appear indefinite. In this
   paper, the author discusses this issue by adopting interval numbers to
   express this kind of indefinite situation. Meanwhile, the least
   deviation method is proposed to calculate the weights of indicators
   according to the interval numbers comparison matrix, which is solved by
   the particle swarm optimization. As a result, this paper provides a kind
   of new thought to similar solutions. The calculated example of corporate
   environmental performance indicator weights indicates that the result is
   very well conformed to the fact and the work is useful in practice.},
