   Management; German Acad Exchange Serv Fdn; German Ind \& Commerce; Off
   European Commiss Hong Kong \& Macao; CSR Asia},
Abstract = {The paper studies the foreign-owned enterprises during the Chinese
   Reformation. The win-win pattern between foreigners and China as long as
   a series of negative news have been investigated. The result reveals
   that some foreign-owned enterprises are lack of social responsibility in
   labor's right, pollution and security problems. The author believes,
   firms are no longer lonely islands for profit maximization simply, but a
   junction in the contract network connecting the individuals, society and
   other enterprise companies compactly. The vague frontier of rights
   between firm and society would make the externality of firms' hurt
   social benefits of the others. The author suggests, when pursuing
   profit, a corporate citizen is simultaneously expected to improve or
   remedy potential problems by repaying society. A campaign of corporation
   social responsibility (CSR) in China is also discussed.},
