   ENVIRONMENTAL MANAGEMENT},
Year = {2007},
Pages = {107+},
Note = {Euro-Asian Conference on Environment and Corporate Social Responsibility
   - Perspectives from Business in Asia, Hong Kong, PEOPLES R CHINA, NOV
   17, 2006},
Organization = {TU Bergakademie Freiberg; Hong Kong Univ, Ctr Urban Planning \& Environm
   Management; German Acad Exchange Serv Fdn; German Ind \& Commerce; Off
   European Commiss Hong Kong \& Macao; CSR Asia},
Abstract = {Many researches have been done on ethical issues in China, but domestic
   researchers ignore that human resources management is also a field full
   of ethical dilemmas. In order to gain sustaining competitiveness,
   companies must secure advantages in human resources and be able to
   attract and keep high level human resources in accordance with human
   resources ethics. This paper introduces the concepts of human resources
   ethics and ethical dilemma, analyzes a case by using a moral principles
   framework, and discusses ways in which companies may be liberated from
   human resources ethical dilemmas, furthermore, the values of human
   resources ethical management is stressed.},
