   17, 2006},
Organization = {TU Bergakademie Freiberg; Hong Kong Univ, Ctr Urban Planning \& Environm
   Management; German Acad Exchange Serv Fdn; German Ind \& Commerce; Off
   European Commiss Hong Kong \& Macao; CSR Asia},
Abstract = {In recent years, Corporate Social Responsibility (CSR) has become one of
   the main issues in business, while cultural management and CSR seem to
   be one of the hot topics for academic studies. China is a country with
   abundant traditional culture which plays a very important role in
   corporate management. This article firstly reviews the theory of CSR,
   and presents the basic content of China traditional culture. Then, it
   analyses the relationship between corporate cultural management and
   corporate social responsibility from the perspective of the Chinese
   traditional culture, studies corporate social ethic and business
   morality based on the traditional culture. The author stresses that
   enterprises' behavior should be a unification of economic man and moral
   person as a social citizen. Finally, a proposal about how to construct
   corporation culture based on corporate social responsibility is
   presented.},
